# The built PWA once lived at the repository root, because GitHub Pages was
# configured to publish the root directory. It is deployed from the Actions
# workflow now, which builds apps/web and uploads only that — so a build at the
# root is a stale duplicate that serves nothing and drifts a little further from
# the real one with every deploy. These are anchored with a leading slash, so
# they only cover the root and leave apps/web/index.html and friends alone.
/index.html
/manifest.webmanifest
/sw.js
/sw.js.map
/workbox-*.js
/workbox-*.js.map
/assets/
/vendor/
/icons/
/launch/
/favicon.svg
/apple-touch-icon.png
/.nojekyll
